From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0276: camera exposure, preview ring, 108 MP still op

kern.sweet_cam_exp: write "lines gain_x1000 [frame_length]" (HM6 0x0202,
0x0204 with 1x = 0x20 up to 64x, 0x0340, inside a 0x0104 group hold, page
0x4000); read the mode, frame/line length, line time and limits. The
exposure time is carried over a mode change.
Op 30 starts a preview (HM6 mode 1 by default, 3 = 1280x720, 4 = 2x crop;
arg bits 4-7) into a ring of four buffers at the pool start: a kernel thread
follows CSID RDI0 SOF/EOF, programs the next buffer into WM7 at each SOF
(latched at the next one) and publishes each finished buffer
(kern.sweet_cam_latest: seq, buffer, offset, size, time); it stops at an SMMU
fault. kern.sweet_cam_sel chooses what kern.sweet_cam_frame reads (-1 the
newest preview frame, 0-3 a buffer, 100 the still). Op 31 stops the preview.
Op 32 stops it, switches to mode 0 and takes one 108 MP frame at the pool
start. Op 9 now also stops the stream, CSID/TFE and turns their clocks off
(the L4/L18 votes stay at UEFI's values: the display and USB PHYs share
them). A CCI failure logs the master's pin levels; the ultra wide's power-up
sets the CSI mux low. HM6 mode 3 joins the generated tables.
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_cam.c        |  481 ++++++++++++-
 bsd/dev/sweet_cam_tables.h | 1624 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 2084 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

